  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats played a full set at the Bowery Ballroom in New York on March 30, 2011, as documented in this recording [1]. The performance is captured through a matrix mix that combines soundboard audio with audience microphones, providing a balanced perspective of the room [1]. This specific upload was originally shared on the nyctaper.com website [1]. The setlist features twenty songs, including the rare tracks \"Seeing Daylight\" and \"Outer Scorpion Squadron\" [1]. Notably, the recording includes \"Matthew\" and \"Snow Crush Goddamn Killing Song,\" both of which are the only archived performances of these songs in the collection [1]. The band also performed \"Age of Kings\" and \"Ontario,\" which are considered rare with only eight and nine archived performances respectively [1]. The show concluded with an encore featuring \"No Children,\" \"This Year,\" and \"The Best Ever Death Metal Band from Denton\" [1]. This is the second consecutive night the band played at the Bowery Ballroom, following a show on March 29, 2011 [2]. As the 155th show in the archive's collection for the band, it offers a comprehensive look at their live presence during that period [2]. The audio is a 92-minute recording that was taped and transferred by nyctaper [1]. Listeners can expect a complete experience of the evening, from the opening \"Liza Forever Minnelli\" to the final encore [1].",
